Subject: [PATCH 02503/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D1
 (ORACLE-DISTINCT ACCURACY complementary measurement; 2026-06-14 P0 MANDATORY)
 -- the verifier-as-DETECTOR measurement. The standing P0 directive: HEADLINE
 = an oracle-distinct learned/energy verifier (the in-generation moat, Phase
 C); COMPLEMENTARY = the verifier-as-DETECTOR measurement (cheap; cached data)
 -- detection AUROC where SELECTION headroom is ~0. This is the cheap,
 infra-INDEPENDENT probe of the oracle-distinct ACCURACY frontier that is NOT
 hostage to the DiffusionGemma infra (which has blocked 3x), diversifying the
 'verifier earns its place' bet across THREE vehicles (efficiency/Phase A,
 in-generation/Phase C, detection/here). Per the spec
 (docs/research-notes/verifier-as-detector-measurement-spec.md): measure
 whether the verifier ensemble DETECTS step-errors (AUROC) on corpora where it
 cannot SELECT a better answer (oracle@K == vote@1, ~0 selection headroom).
 Emit detector_auroc BARE float + detector_beats_chance BARE bool (AUROC CI95
 lower bound > 0.5). verifier_is_oracle=false (a learned/energy detection
 signal, oracle-distinct). Cached candidates, no live LLM. If a prior detector
 measurement exists, EXTEND it to a NEW corpus/condition (no churn). NO TRM
 training.

